  "lineage": "Shyama sangeet are Bengali Shakta devotional songs addressed to the goddess Kali (Shyama), a genre shaped in the eighteenth century by Ramprasad Sen, whose plain 'Ramprasadi' tunes became a model, and continued by Kamalakanta Bhattacharya and later by Kazi Nazrul Islam. In the gramophone era it became a staple of Calcutta recording, sung solo with harmonium and tabla.",
